1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Hi. In this video, we'll look at how you can use Burp Suite to bypass client-side controls.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Some applications rely on measures on the client side to control the data that they submit to the server.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:24,000
This can lead to significant security flaws, as the user has full control over the client.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:32,000
To restrict user input, applications use a range of mechanisms that prevent the user from directly seeing and modifying data.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:40,000
You can use Burp Proxy to intercept a request, then modify data in the HTTP request before forwarding it to the server.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
This enables you to change data in a way that may not have been possible in the application.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
You can follow along using the lab Excessive Trust in Client-Side Controls from our Web Security Academy.

8
00:00:52,000 --> 00:01:01,000
To view and modify data in Burp in order to bypass client-side controls, first access the page for the function you want to test in Burp's browser.

9
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,000
In the lab, we'll go to the product page for the leather jacket.

10
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:14,000
And then, in Burp, go to the Proxy Intercept tab and click on Intercept is off to toggle Interception on.

11
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:18,000
In Burp's browser, we can now click through the function.

12
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Burp intercepts each request.

13
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
The message details are shown in the Intercept tab.

14
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
We can review each request for interesting content.

15
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:32,000
For example, look for parameters that are hidden on the web page.

16
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:35,000
In this example, we can see there's a hidden price parameter.

17
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Then, edit the message.

18
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:39,000
So we're going to edit the price.

19
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:44,000
Once you've made your changes, click forward to send the request.

20
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:51,000
We can now turn Interception back off again and determine whether the modification was successfully updated on the server side.

21
00:01:51,000 --> 00:02:08,000
We can do this by checking the Proxy HTTP history tab and finding the request we just edited from the edited column and reviewing the response.

22
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,000
You can also review the website.

23
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,000
In this lab, we can view the cart and see that the price has successfully changed.

24
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:15,000
We can view the cart and see that the price has successfully changed.

25
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,000
We can view the cart and see that the price has successfully changed.

